ame":"yt-attributed-string","type":"FRAME","scrollBehavior":"SCROLLS","children":[{"id":"75:24493","name":"My husband and I hav","type":"TEXT","scrollBehavior":"SCROLLS","blendMode":"PASS_THROUGH","fills":[{"blendMode":"NORMAL","type":"SOLID","color":{"r":0.05882352963089943,"g":0.05882352963089943,"b":0.05882352963089943,"a":1}},{"blendMode":"NORMAL","type":"SOLID","color":{"r":0.9450980424880981,"g":0.9450980424880981,"b":0.9450980424880981,"a":1}}],"strokes":[],"strokeWeight":1,"strokeAlign":"OUTSIDE","absoluteBoundingBox":{"x":1998.1639404296875,"y":5654.9921875,"width":1205,"height":137},"absoluteRenderBounds":{"x":1998.5809326171875,"y":5656.3486328125,"width":1200.8419189453125,"height":77.1435546875},"constraints":{"vertical":"TOP","horizontal":"LEFT"},"characters":"My husband and I have seen the black triangle craft and I’m so glad they were mentioned here. It actually wasn’t too long ago, November 8th, 2:14AM 2024, Mesa Arizona. We were both walking our dogs (we work night shift and walk them late) around our apartment complex. When I first stepped outside I noticed you could see far more stars than normal and was fascinated, living in the city you hardly see any. So as the dogs sniffed around in the grass we stared up at the sky as I pointed out the red star Betelgeuse to him. When suddenly a big black triangle craft flew quickly and silently overhead. It was much lower than any plane or helicopter (we live near a hospital and get a lot of helicopters) and it had 3 orange lights on each corner. The lights looked as though they shone through a mist or a haze, even though it was a clear cloudless night. We only saw it for a few short seconds before it was gone, it was so fast.\nWe didn’t know what it was, but the moment I saw it I got a sinking feeling in my stomach and all I could think was “they’re real.”\nStill don’t know what to think, government or aliens, but I hope I learn the truth one day.","characterStyleOverrides":[],"styleOverrideTable":{},"line